>> title: Frozen Prawns in Garlic Butter, Air Fryer
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: frozen, prawns, shrimp, air fryer, basket, weeknight
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> aka: air fryer frozen shrimp, frozen prawns, garlic butter shrimp, air fryer shrimp from frozen, frozen prawns in butter
>> servings: 4
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: narrow — a prawn curls into a C when it is done and a tight O when it is over, and the ninety seconds between the two is the whole recipe
>> washing-up: the basket, the bowl
>> keeps: not at all — reheating turns a prawn to rubber, which is the one thing this recipe was avoiding

>> step: Straight from the freezer into a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. A 3.5 L basket is two batches.
Frozen and dry. Thawed prawns weep into the basket and steam.

>> step: toss them frozen in the bowl they come back to
Toss @frozen raw prawns{1%lb}(450 g; peeled and deveined, straight from the freezer) in a #bowl{} with @olive oil{1%Tbs}, @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{1%tsp}.

>> step: roast in the basket 200°C (400°F), 8–10 min, one layer
Roast @&(~1)frozen prawns{} in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 200°C (400°F) for ~air fry{9%min}, one layer and not touching.

>> step: toss the basket at five minutes — curled to a C, not a tight O
Toss @&(~1)prawns{} by shaking the basket once.

>> step: toss hot in the same bowl, the prawns melt the butter
Toss @&(~1)prawns{} with @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(cubed cold), @garlic{2%cloves}(grated), @red chile flakes{1/2%tsp}, @lemon{1/2}(juiced), @parsley{2%Tbs}(chopped).
